This is a textbook case of **coverage-without-verification** — every production method is called, giving ~95% line coverage, but almost nothing is actually asserted. Here's the severity-ranked audit:

---

## 🔴 Critical — Missing Assertions (coverage inflation)

### 1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17) — **Fire-and-forget, zero verification**
Calls `AddProduct` but never checks the product was stored.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(stored);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

### 2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32) — **Mutation never verified**
Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price actually changed. A no-op implementation would pass.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

### 3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38) — **Deletion never verified**
Calls `RemoveProduct` but never checks the product is gone. A no-op `Delete` passes this test.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

### 4. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68) — **Bulk mutation completely unverified**
Applies a 10% discount to two products but never checks any price changed. This is your highest-risk gap — discount math bugs ship silently.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

### 5. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63) — **Return value discarded**
Calls `GetProductCount()` on an empty catalog and throws away the result. Not even an `IsNotNull` here.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
```

### 6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84) — **Round-trip never checked**
Imports a CSV row but never verifies a product was actually created or that fields parsed correctly.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var p = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(p);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", p.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, p.Price);
```

---

## 🟠 High — Weak Assertions (assert-not-null-and-stop)

### 7. `GetProduct_Works` (line 22) — **Only checks non-null**
